// URL-loaded customization: usTimeClusters
//
// Problem: an ultrasound series holds single images from several sweeps, and
// each image records its acquisition time. The default rules put all of the
// single images in one stack, so the sweeps mix.
//
// Fix: each sweep - a run of images with no gap in time longer than 20
// seconds - becomes its own display set, in time order.
//
// How it works:
//  - The default display set context has the group `timeClusters` (the
//    built-in series function). It reads AcquisitionDateTime, else
//    AcquisitionDate and AcquisitionTime, else ContentDate and ContentTime,
//    sorts the times, and starts a new cluster after a gap of more than
//    `timeClustersMaxGap` seconds. `sweepStart` is the start time of the
//    cluster of the instance, and `sweepCount` is the number of clusters.
//  - The rule `context` sets `timeClustersMaxGap` to 20 for this rule only.
//    Other rules keep the default gap of 30 seconds.
//  - `matches` claims the single-frame US images that have a time, and only
//    in a series with two or more sweeps. Multi-frame clips stay with the
//    default `multiFrame` rule. The clips still count in the time clusters,
//    so a clip can join two sweeps into one.
//  - `groupBy` uses the start time of the cluster. A cluster keeps its key
//    when a later cluster gets new instances. The natural order of the keys
//    puts the display sets in time order.
//  - `sortBy` orders the images of a sweep by time.
//  - `attributes` adds the start of the sweep (`sweepOffset`, in seconds from
//    the first image of the series) to the SeriesDescription.
//
// Series that this module changes: US series whose single images form two or
// more sweeps. A series of one sweep keeps the default display sets.
//
// Load it with `?customization=split/usTimeClusters`.
{
  "requires": ["split/enableNewSplit"],
  "global": {
    "useMetadataDisplaySet": {
      "splitRules": {
        "$merge": {
          "usTimeClusters": {
            "priority": -1,
            "description": "Ultrasound single images: one display set for each sweep of contiguous acquisition time.",
            "context": { "timeClustersMaxGap": 20 },
            "matches": {
              "isImage": true,
              "Modality": "US",
              "isMultiFrame": false,
              "sweepCount": { "greaterThan": 1 },
              "sweepStart": { "notNull": true }
            },
            "groupBy": ["SeriesInstanceUID", "sweepStart"],
            "sortBy": ["acquisitionSeconds"],
            "attributes": {
              "SeriesDescription": { "template": "{SeriesDescription} +{sweepOffset} s" }
            }
          }
        }
      }
    }
  }
}
